{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "04YK", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-immersions}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2809f30de8126e09d9c505c6f5525ebba4b8c31aabc03765d175b4947438f282", "source_text": "Immersions of algebraic stacks", "source_text_hash": "sha256:245be5d6fbd288df7010cf9f907bfa6038b1c02bee6c9c02b5ec379e362ca097", "unit_id": "tag:04YK:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04YK", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e708ff49135e162d207aa2d0346704778e9d8c0acae311c0a940fafcbe948abf", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nImmersions of algebraic stacks are defined as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e2aa0db7a38816397466e8664898cd0a768f84cdcbf19d7d1171d3b628c5fed6", "unit_id": "tag:04YK:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04YK", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{section-properties-morphisms}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{section-properties-morphisms}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-immersion}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6210b9d13d827f1099e5b1a47e41959465354afd527d79d1aeeef2adae54b0b7", "source_text": "Immersions.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> A morphism of algebraic stacks is called an <TEXTITOPEN_0001>open immersion<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif it is representable, and an open immersion\nin the sense of\nSection <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0003> A morphism of algebraic stacks is called a <TEXTITOPEN_0002>closed immersion<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nif it is representable, and a closed immersion\nin the sense of\nSection <REF_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0004> A morphism of algebraic stacks is called an <TEXTITOPEN_0003>immersion<TEXTITCLOSE_0003>\nif it is representable, and an immersion\nin the sense of\nSection <REF_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:81745b6acc2c3ec2e6ec3488dd1a692207a811260c364510c990a264c0a7416c", "unit_id": "tag:04YL:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04YK", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:597e1efe298fd194f5e65fbd85f00e4aeacbd7e67c4ae406cddc43f28081a117", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is not the most convenient way to think about immersions for us.\nFor us it is a little bit more convenient to think of an immersion\nas a morphism of algebraic stacks which is representable by algebraic\nspaces and is an immersion in the sense of\nSection <REF_0001>.\nSimilarly for closed and open immersions.\nSince this is clearly equivalent to the notion just defined we shall\nuse this characterization without further mention.\nWe prove a few simple lemmas about this notion.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1a7abed20655dc515f48afdda1b5aa01333832f94349ea67e36e869b88ab8bbc", "unit_id": "tag:04YK:prose-0002"}
